[15:02.87]Recording One
[15:05.88]If you're away from home, feeling a bit blue or searching for some comfort, the Danes have a solution.
[15:15.02]It's called "hygge," and it's becoming a sensation around the globe.
[15:20.46]Emerging from Danish culture, but popularized by the British in 2016, hygge is much more than just a word.
[15:30.04]It is a whole world of customs and behaviors designed to make people feel good together.
[15:37.24]The hygge concept is hard to define.
[15:40.19]It refers to the sense of well-being you get when your family is gathered together at New Year or Christmas.
[15:47.80]It is all about the pleasant sensations of home: the scents of your mother's cooking, your partner's arm around your shoulder, a warm mug of tea in your hand and so on.
[15:59.99]If you want to feel what hygge is like, light a few candles and settle in for a cozy evening on the sofa, perhaps listening to some soft music.
[16:11.14]Hygge is an antidote to stress.
[16:13.67]It is impossible to measure, but you know when you've got it because a gentle warmth starts spreading through your body.
[16:21.67]Another important part of hygge is that it does not involve modern technology.
[16:27.37]It's a digital detox designed to relax your exhausted mind and eyes.
[16:32.93]So, put down your smartphone and turn off the computer.
[16:36.88]They are definitely not hygge.
[16:39.48]What you need to do if you want to get down with the Danes is to imagine yourself back in earlier times, sitting in front of a blazing fire and listening to your granddad telling a story as the smell of something delicious coming out from the kitchen.
[16:56.23]Imagine the restful calm and peace.
[16:59.22]You should also know that hygge is not about healthy eating or crazy exercise regimes.
[17:06.26]In fact, it's just the opposite.
[17:09.03]You're supposed to indulge in a little bit of what you fancy: some naughty-but-nice treats.
[17:14.94]So, sugary snacks and calorie-laden cakes are in.
[17:19.08]Let yourself be carried on a wave of nostalgia back to your birthplace, and remember with a smile the old nursery rhymes and childhood songs of your distant youth.
[17:30.90]If it helps, wrap yourself in a warm blanket and cuddle up with one of your favorite books.
[17:36.86]If Denmark seems too remote, then picture yourself huddled around a traditional stove with your loved ones, chatting about the old days.
[17:46.53]Let yourself drift back in time to a period where nothing is urgent, and there is no need to respond to any emails or text messages.
[17:55.56]They did not exist back then.
[17:59.49]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.
